<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Harmony buys remaining Lydex shares.</title>
<headline>Harmony buys remaining Lydex shares.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harmony Gold Mining Co Ltd has acquired all the shares held by Lydenburg Exploration Ltd shareholders that were not bought following an offer set out in a notice dated December 12, 1996, the firms said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The remining shares were bought for a cash payment of 10 rand a share, together with 45 Harmony options for every 100 Lydex shares held, they said.</p>
<p>Consequently the listing of Lydex's shares on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange will be terminated on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
